WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.420
Lü Bu's army clashed with the allied forces
of Liu Bei and Cao Cao.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:08.080
Guan Yu, who was greatly impressed

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.880
by the way Zhang Liao fought gallantly
as a general in Lü Bu's army,

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.500
pleaded that his life be spared.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.210
Then, several years later,

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:20.080
Guan Yu, who had been cornered by Cao Cao's army,

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.670
refused to surrender,
instead choosing to end his own life.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:26.170
However, Zhang Liao pleaded with him
until he agreed to surrender.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:30.500
It is said that afterward the two
continued to foster their friendship.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.040
Now, back to the present.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.170
Here, too, a certain close friendship has begun to form.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.670
In street performances with Nanami,
Eiko does her best to find herself.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:44.250
<i>I wanna sing with my own voice like Nanamin does.</i>

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:47.460
The two hang out a lot beyond just performing

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.830
and have gradually established an emotional bond.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:52.710
I hope we can keep on laughing together, Nanamin!

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:57.080
Hoping to broaden the ways in which
she can express herself just as Nanami has,

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:00.380
Eiko earnestly continues to sing.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:03.580
Eiko, the way you performed just now was amazing.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:08.130
Having finally obtained her own voice,
Eiko rushed to see Kido.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:13.580
The close friendship that has blossomed between
the two girls will keep going strong.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.330
Or so it seems.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.000
Chance x Chance, Rendezvous!! Chiki chiki ban ban

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:33.000
<b><i>ya Boy KONGMING!</i></b>

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.830
Pity?! Chiki chiki chan chan

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.710
Ah! Chiki chiki ban ban

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:33.580
Love!! Chuki chuki chuki ban ban

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.420
High chiki chiki ban ban

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.290
Pity?! Chiki chiki chan chan

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.130
Ah! Chiki chiki ban ban

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:40.000
Love!! Chuki chuki

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:47.210
Everyone and his brother is fickle and it's so trying

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:50.880
If you get drunk on tequila

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.670
With a string of groundless fantasies, flash

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:56.420
Dreams are Pandora

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.880
See? You get an urge to open them

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:02.040
Expect good things from everybody, party people

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.500
You won't understand unless you climb Mt. Fuji tonight

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.880
The showdown is the destiny of the weekend

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.920
Chance x Chance, Rendezvous!! Chiki chiki ban ban

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:16.130
Enjoy yourself without being pretentious about anything

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:17.830
Fever tonight

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:20.500
Chance x Chance, Pity?! Chiki chiki ban ban

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:25.330
No matter how often you're irritated, party tonight

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:28.130
Chance x Chance, Ah! Chiki chiki ban ban

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:32.830
A perfect society were the stupider you act, the greater the high

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.500
Chance x Chance, Love!! Chiki chiki ban ban

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:40.420
Everybody is a superstar in the making, diva tonight

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.630
<b>KARASAWA</b>

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.630
<b>Message</b>

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.630
<b>Remind Me</b>

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:56.710
Hello.

00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:01.880
Kuon, I hear you've been singing on the streets lately.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.210
How do you...

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:07.040
I shouldn't have to tell you this, but stop immediately.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.580
Furthermore, it seems there's a girl
who've been singing with.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.250
I don't want you seeing her ever again.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:18.960
Get back here in time for the meeting.

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:20.420
You got that?

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.710
<b>For the Populace</b>

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:33.040
Cause you gave me whispers of love all night

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:38.420
How was it?

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:40.500
Good.

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:43.420
But you still have a long way to go.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:45.920
Though you've improved,

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:48.500
what lies at your very core...

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.580
what it is that you're singing for...

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.960
Until you find out, it won't make the grade.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.420
How'd it go?

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:03.880
He said it won't make the grade
until I figure out what I'm singing for.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.750
Aww, I've got no idea what to do.

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:12.630
Listen, you're singing with your own voice now, Eiko!

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.380
Trust me, not that pudding geezer!

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.500
Thanks!

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.210
Ah, I know!

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:25.130
How about we go somewhere to unwind?

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.500
Unwind, huh?

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:29.170
Oh, that pouch from Kongming...

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:34.210
A ticket for the observation deck at Sky Square.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:40.130
That alone's a waste, wanna get to the next place

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.880
I want my skills to be profound

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.880
Ain’t no throwaway round,
we circle up and wanna go down

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.250
Yay!

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:48.080
Thanks a ton, guys!

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.330
I never imagined you'd all turn up for this!

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:51.830
You bet your ass we would!

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:55.790
After all, we've got our hometown hero sayin'
he's gonna battle Sekitoba again!

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:57.210
We wanna support you!

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:59.960
We'll hang with you every day if ya want.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:01.330
Right, Sasatcho?

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:02.330
Yeah!

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:06.500
Besides, this time of day my job's done,
and I have nothin' to do for fun.

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:08.750
I see, you've got it rough.

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:10.830
Hey, wait a minute!

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.380
My job's done...
nothin' to do for fun...

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.420
Sasatcho, did you just bust a rhyme?!

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:19.540
I had to since you said
I didn't make a single one last time.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:24.380
A casual challenge, met with unbelievable talent

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:26.460
Ah, you rhymed right back at me!

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:30.460
Sasatcho! It's brazen of you to
pick a fight with Kabetaijin!

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:32.880
Ah, forgive me!
I can't compete with thee!

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:34.670
I need to go take a wee

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:36.540
Wow, you rhymed three words!

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:39.380
Yeah, but they were pretty lame rhymes.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:42.330
Aw, come on, man!
This's who I am!

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:44.420
What's wrong?

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:45.960
Ah, it's nothing at all!

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:46.630
Nothing at all, no need to bawl

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:47.920
<i>This is me, huh?
</i>Nothing at all, no need to bawl<b></b>

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:49.130
<i>This is me, huh?
</i>My YouTube's still small, y'all<b></b>

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:50.540
My YouTube's still small, y'all

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:53.830
Seriously, man?!

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:58.580
Wow, we're so high up!

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.250
Now this is exciting!

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:03.290
Oh, a blimp!

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:10.460
Hey, Nanamin, do you think about
something when you sing?

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:12.170
Like, what it is you're singing for?

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:13.710
Me?

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:17.420
I guess I don't really think about anything.

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:19.170
I just do it 'cause I like it.

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:20.960
On the streets, anyway.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.920
On the streets?

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:25.250
I had a feeling!

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.290
You must be a pro, right?!

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:28.670
You're just too darn good!

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:31.290
Well, you could say I'm a pro.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.630
I don't show my face, though.

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:34.040
I knew it!

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.830
You give the impression of being in the biz!

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:37.580
Are you a studio musician?

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:40.380
Oh, or maybe a tour member with someone famous?!

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:42.830
Wow, look at that!

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:44.330
Whoa, it's so close!

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.750
Sure enough, I think I better tell you, Eiko.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:52.670
After all, this might be the last time we meet.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.880
Um, what?

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:00.000
I'm sorry.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.290
I should have told you sooner,

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:06.130
but I just wanted to be myself around you.

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:10.040
Ta-da!

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:13.540
I'm the idol band Azalea's bassist and vocalist:

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:16.130
Nanami Kuon.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:19.630
Ugh, how lame.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:22.580
No way...

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:28.670
Ya Boy Kongming!

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:27.080
<b><i>ya</i></b>

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:27.630
<b><i>ya Boy</i></b>

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:27.830
<b><i>ya Boy KONG</i></b>

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:29.960
<b><i>ya Boy KONGMING!</i></b>

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:33.580
Nanamin, you're in Azalea?

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.290
You've gotta be kidding.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:40.250
I mean, you're nothing like those girls.

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:46.040
At first, things were different.

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:49.330
<b>Music Room</b>

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:52.500
Wow, your drumming was perfect, Futaba!

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.500
Thanks! You were great too, Ichika.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.420
Hey, was I good?

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:58.420
Of course!

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:01.080
Your singing and bass playing is key, Nanami.

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:04.460
Ah, I can't wait for the school festival.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:08.960
We've never performed for an audience,
so I'm a bit nervous.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.790
Well, we all feel that way!

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.130
It'll be okay!

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:14.380
Yeah, you're right!

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:16.250
What's wrong?!

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:17.920
That reminds me!

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:19.630
We haven't decided on a name for our band!

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:20.830
You're right!

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:23.420
We got so caught up in practicing we totally forgot!

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:27.130
Well then, let's each come up with a suggestion.

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:30.460
What?! You go first then at least, Nanami.

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:31.670
Okay.

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:35.290
How about: "Band, Band, Band"?!

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:36.500
Rejected.

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:39.080
Why'd you suggest "Band, Band, Band"?

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.420
There are three of us, so...

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:41.710
Band! Band! Band!

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:44.580
Hey, can I go next?

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:48.960
We take part of Nanami, Ichika, and Futaba to make:

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.250
"Nanaichiba"!

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.500
Whaddaya think?!

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:53.460
Oh, not bad!

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:54.460
Right?!

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:56.580
So, Futaba, you got anything?

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:00.460
Yeah, I actually had a name in mind.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:03.960
What do you think about "Azalea"?

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:08.790
"Azalea"? What's that mean?

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:12.080
It's the name of a flower.

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:17.000
And in the language of flowers,
they mean the joy of youth.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:19.540
I like it!

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:25.250
<i>I started a band with my high school friends,
and we played the music we wanted to play.</i>

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:27.540
That's great! Really great!

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:31.290
<i>We had our debut concert on the school festival stage.</i>

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:36.210
Amazing!

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:37.580
You were super cool!

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:41.960
Wow, this is crazy...

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:46.710
That was the best thing ever!

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:48.880
Jeez, I've still got goosebumps!

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:51.380
Yeah, that was so emotional!

00:09:54.540 --> 00:10:00.290
For the rest of high school, and even after I graduate,
I'm gonna keep making music!

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:03.250
So, won't you two join me?!

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:06.790
Hey, we're still first-years, you know!

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:09.960
We don't know where we'll be that far in the future!

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:13.290
Oh, come on!
You saying you don't wanna?!

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:18.250
You better believe we do!

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:23.210
All right, this is just the start for Azalea!

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:30.210
From then on, music was at the center
of our high school lives.

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:35.670
Then, after we graduated, the three of us moved
to Tokyo together for the sake of our music.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:37.880
Oh, I see.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:42.670
But even after moving here,
no good opportunities came our way.

00:10:43.170 --> 00:10:45.920
Besides, we never drew crowds when we played gigs.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:50.500
Even so, we were still having fun at that point.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:54.500
After all, we'd been able
to keep playing music we loved.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:56.000
At that point?

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:01.540
<i>Until he showed up, that is.</i>

00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:04.170
<b>Producer</b>

00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:04.170
<b>Toshihiko Karasawa</b>

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:08.540
So, what kind of music do you want to perform?

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:10.960
Without a doubt, rock!

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:13.380
Stuff that really moves everyone who hears it!

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:17.210
Yeah! After all, we've always played hard-hitting music!

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:22.290
Plus, in flower language Azalea
represents the joy of youth!

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:27.920
So, we wanna express the feeling of excitement
we had we when first started the band.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:30.380
Yeah! Well said, Futaba!

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:32.290
What hogwash.

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.290
You don't know jack, after all.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.170
You formed three years ago.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:42.500
If you can't even halfway fill a
50-person-capacity venue...

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:45.960
just quit already!

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:47.880
A band like that won't sell.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:50.630
What's it to you anyway?!

00:11:50.630 --> 00:11:52.330
I'm not finished yet.

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:54.670
I'm offering you a chance.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:55.880
A chance?

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:58.540
Sing my songs,

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:01.540
and I'll have you doing a big-time
dome tour within two years.

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:03.080
Domes?

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:04.580
Within two years?

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:09.880
If you let this opportunity pass you by,
you will never make it big.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.000
What are you talking about?

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:15.960
Go screw yourself!

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:19.790
An unpolished gem does not sparkle.

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:29.670
Think this over carefully.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.210
Who does he think he is calling us over for that?!

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:37.540
Like hell I'd sing his damn songs!

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:39.920
I hate his stupid songs, too!

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:46.080
Still, all the stuff Karasawa produces
has been successful.

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:48.460
Listen, our big chance will come someday!

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:51.420
Yeah, right on!
Let's keep on doing our thing!

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.040
You're right!

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:54.960
Yeah!

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:58.290
<i>We believed in our music.</i>

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:00.130
<i>But...</i>

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:04.960
<i>we didn't know how to find a market for it.</i>

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:10.630
There are still unsold tickets.
We've gotta pay and take a loss again.

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:13.210
Ah! I need to pick up more part-time work!

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:16.210
Just living in Tokyo costs a lot.

00:13:16.210 --> 00:13:18.710
No way in hell I'm moving back to the countryside!

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:20.670
<b>Part-Time Job Recruitment</b>

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:20.670
<b>BAITORE</b>

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:28.670
<b>Bankbook</b>

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:28.670
<b>ICHIKA</b>

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:30.540
<i>We were barely getting by.</i>

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:34.880
Well, I've gotta head to work now.

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:36.290
Me, too.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.250
<i>And so...</i>

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:43.920
Hello.

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:46.420
This Nanami Kuon from Azalea.

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:51.130
I'm very sorry for being so rude earlier!

00:13:51.670 --> 00:13:53.790
Please, make us successful!

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:55.580
Now, that's better.

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:58.830
I, too, once misunderstood the way of things.

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:02.500
I thought I could make a living doing what I liked.

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:07.040
However, one's compensation
is tied to pleasing others.

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:10.080
I had failed to understand that basic concept.

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:12.250
Don't you worry.

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:15.460
Rest assured I'll turn you girls into stars.

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:18.080
Yes, sir! Please and thank you!

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:28.250
What's with this outfit?

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:30.710
This is the new costume for Azalea.

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:33.790
Starting today, it's what you'll be wearing.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.670
I could never! There's no way!

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:37.920
Right, Nanami?!

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:40.500
Nanami?

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:42.580
They are sure to be a hit.

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:46.880
You must follow all my instructions
on your dress, songs, and choreography.

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:48.670
If you want to make it big...

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:50.460
wear them!

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:52.500
For real?

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:55.920
These are part of your costumes as well.

00:14:56.420 --> 00:15:00.790
As of today, you girls will be reborn as the new Azalea.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:03.210
Nanami, what are we gonna do?!

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:06.540
This will make us popular, right?

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:09.540
Yes, of that I am sure.

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:14.960
What we wear won't change who we are.

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:18.130
For now, just suck it up and wear it.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:20.250
Seriously?

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:22.880
If you say so, Nanami...

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:28.080
<i>Just as Karasawa had promised,
we got more fans in no time.</i>

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:30.460
Once again, we're Azalea!

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:38.750
Hold it right there!

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:39.960
What are you saying?!

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:44.500
In short, from your next gig on,
you can just pretend to sing and play.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.130
Use that energy to concentrate
on your performances.

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:49.210
That's what the audience wants to see.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:50.670
B-but...

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.960
We've always been a real band...

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:57.500
<i>From then on, we continued to do
whatever Karasawa told us to.</i>

00:15:58.130 --> 00:15:59.330
<i>And as a result...</i>

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:06.500
<i>...our fanbase exploded.</i>

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:08.540
<i>We sold loads of CDs and merch,</i>

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:12.290
<i>and we became able to make a living on music alone.</i>

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:16.580
<i>That said...</i>

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:18.580
Did you see the payment we got this month?

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:19.580
Yep!

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.580
I had a dishwasher shipped to my parents' place!

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:24.460
Hey, so about that last gig...

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:37.040
Now that you mention it,
I bought a new microwave myself!

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:38.290
Oh, seriously?!

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:41.830
Nice! Maybe I should buy some new appliances, too.

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:45.710
Oh? You're already heading home, Nanami?

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:48.920
Yeah, I'm gonna go out and sing to unwind.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:50.420
I see...

00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:59.460
<i>That change in clothing had, in fact, changed me.</i>

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:04.170
But it was when I sang with you, Eiko,
that I knew for sure...

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:08.250
I no longer want to sing Karasawa's songs.

00:17:08.830 --> 00:17:12.580
But Azalea is no longer just about us three.

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:15.380
We have a whole team and lots of money behind us.

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:20.130
I don't wanna betray our staff who promote us
or our fans who come see us.

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:23.460
I'm sorry for keeping it from you.

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:30.290
I've got something I need to tell you too, Nanamin.

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:36.500
That 100,000 Likes Project where a ticket
to Summer Sonia is on the line...

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:38.790
I'm in the running, too.

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:43.210
I see...

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:45.670
Well, you are a great singer, after all.

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:57.790
<i>Nanamin, you had so much weighing on you all along.</i>

00:17:58.830 --> 00:18:01.000
<i>I totally failed to notice.</i>

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:04.670
<i>All that time it was you giving me courage.</i>

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:07.500
<i>In that case...</i>

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:10.670
All right!

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:12.580
I'm gonna sing!

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:13.920
Huh? Here?

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:16.080
I'm going to sing!

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:17.790
Okay...

00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:26.460
<i>Besides just Nanamin...</i>

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:32.380
<i>I wonder if all the people in this city
have their own worries?</i>

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:35.710
<i>I've sure had my share of troubles.</i>

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:39.540
<i>But music saved me.</i>

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:44.330
<i>So, maybe my singing can save
somebody else out there!</i>

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:48.670
<i>Perhaps I can even save Nanamin
from her current situation!</i>

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:56.460
Everything seemed to be alright

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:02.830
Cause you gave me whispers of love all night

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:08.380
But I'm alone tonight

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:14.250
And I don't know how to stop heaving sighs

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:18.330
I just wanna get you out of my mind

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:21.460
You don't know how much I love you

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:25.580
But you don't wanna be with me any more

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:28.630
I'm still alive today

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:31.540
You are so far away

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:37.210
Even though you have broken my heart, baby

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:40.080
I'm still alive today

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:42.920
And miss you all day

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:49.170
I just thought I could not live without you

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:54.210
Now I don't know what to do with myself

00:19:54.210 --> 00:20:00.080
Maybe I'm stronger than I think and I'm still in...

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:04.580
<i>Reach her!</i>

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:06.210
<i>Reach...</i>

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:08.080
<i>Nanamin's heart!</i>

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:12.830
<i>Nanamin...</i>

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:16.290
<i>Now I see, so this is...</i>

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:20.000
I'm still alive today

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:18.670
<i>the populace!</i>

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:23.130
And miss you all day

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:24.250
<i>To sing for someone's sake...</i>

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:28.580
I just thought I could not live without you

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:27.330
<i>Isn't that right, Kongming?!</i>

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:31.630
I'm still alive today

00:20:31.630 --> 00:20:34.460
You are so far away

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:40.000
Even though you have broken my heart, baby

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:39.710
Eiko, to think you can sing like this...

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:43.000
I'm still alive today

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.830
And miss you all day

00:20:45.830 --> 00:20:52.250
I just thought I could not live without you

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:56.380
Now I don't know what to do with myself

00:20:57.290 --> 00:21:07.630
Maybe I'm stronger than I think and I'm still in love

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:15.330
Wonderful!

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:26.330
I'm also being helped out by a lot of different people.

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:28.750
So, I have no right to be high and mighty.

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:31.380
But there is one thing I can say with confidence!

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:35.750
I love the Nanamin who sings on the streets!

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:38.290
Eiko...

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:52.250
<b>KARASAWA</b>

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:51.710
<i>Karasawa!</i>

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:01.250
Sorry...

00:22:02.170 --> 00:22:03.960
I've gotta go.

00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:07.710
Nanamin!

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:12.290
Thank you for that song.

00:22:13.210 --> 00:22:16.750
But the next time we meet, it might be as rivals.

00:22:18.040 --> 00:22:19.750
Let's both do our best.

00:22:19.960 --> 00:22:21.170
Nanamin!

00:22:21.330 --> 00:22:22.540
Goodbye.

00:22:23.710 --> 00:22:27.460
Nanamin! Let's sing together again sometime!

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:35.710
Nanamin...

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:42.210
Kongming?!

00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:43.540
Don't startle me like that!

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:45.250
You should've told me you were here!

00:22:45.250 --> 00:22:46.460
Please excuse me.

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:49.500
I was so deeply touched that I
unwittingly revealed myself.

00:22:50.040 --> 00:22:54.830
Just then, I observed closely as you sang, Eiko.

00:22:55.250 --> 00:22:57.880
It seems you've found the answer
you were searching for.

00:22:58.630 --> 00:23:01.080
Uh, well...

00:23:01.670 --> 00:23:04.080
I don't know if it's the right one, though.

00:23:12.250 --> 00:23:14.170
The populace, right?!

00:23:17.130 --> 00:23:18.540
Well done!

00:23:27.540 --> 00:23:32.420
Now then, let us venture to new heights.
